{
   "id": "ITM-AGT-01008-05",
   "archetype_id": "BC-QA-01008",
   "variant_id": null,
   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let s be defined by s(x) = k^2 sin(x) for x < pi/2, s(pi/2) = 2k^2 - 3k - 10, and s(x) = cos(x) + k + 20 for x > pi/2, where k is a constant. For what value of k is s continuous at x = pi/2?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 5
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The left-hand limit at x = pi/2 is k^2 sin(pi/2) = k^2 and the right-hand limit is cos(pi/2) + k + 20 = k + 20.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Power",
               "k",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "k",
               20
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Equal one-sided limits need k^2 - k - 20 = 0, so k = 5 or k = -4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Power",
                  "k",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Negate",
                  "k"
               ],
               -20
            ],
            0
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The common limit must also equal s(pi/2) = 2k^2 - 3k - 10. At k = -4 the limit is 16 but s(pi/2) = 34, while at k = 5 the limit is 25 and s(pi/2) = 25.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  2,
                  [
                     "Power",
                     "k",
                     2
                  ]
               ],
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  -3,
                  "k"
               ],
               -10
            ],
            25
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Only k = 5 makes s continuous at x = pi/2.",
         "mathjson": 5
      }
   ],
